late(110.59375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(169.909912 42.952615) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(115.296875 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(253.702963 28.940308) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" d=\"M 3482 4749 Q 3546 4749 3565 4729 Q 3584 4710 3578 4653 L 3552 4307 Q 3546 4262 3536 4249 Q 3526 4237 3462 4237 L 1286 4237 Q 1210 4237 1210 4166 L 1094 2778 Q 1088 2733 1113 2710 Q 1139 2688 1171 2701 Q 1408 2822 1648 2915 Q 1888 3008 2234 3008 Q 2656 3008 3021 2854 Q 3386 2701 3606 2381 Q 3827 2061 3827 1555 Q 3827 1043 3593 681 Q 3360 320 2947 128 Q 2534 -64 2003 -64 Q 1517 -64 1085 105 Q 653 275 352 602 Q 326 640 323 669 Q 320 698 365 730 L 640 954 Q 691 992 749 934 Q 922 774 1088 652 Q 1254 531 1456 464 Q 1658 397 1926 397 Q 2342 397 2630 544 Q 2918 691 3072 950 Q 3226 1210 3226 1536 Q 3226 1882 3078 2102 Q 2931 2323 2684 2432 Q 2438 2541 2138 2541 Q 1798 2541 1529 2419 Q 1261 2298 1037 2163 Q 986 2138 973 2144 Q 960 2150 922 2170 L 608 2349 Q 550 2381 553 2397 Q 557 2413 563 2490 L 736 4659 Q 742 4717 764 4733 Q 787 4749 877 4749 L 3482 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(93 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(336.332888 33.611077) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(93 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pc7fec62301\"><rect x=\"45.676437\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Station speed (cases per hour)","note":null},"answer":"<p>The filler is slowest at 100 cases an hour: 100 × 3,800 = 380k cases a year. After 97% yield: <b>368.6k</b>.</p> <p>Demand is 400k, so Riverbend loses about <b>31.4k cases</b> a year: $126k of contribution.</p>"},{"q":"The upgrade makes the filler 17% faster. What happens?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Filler: 100 × 1.17 = 117 an hour. Now the <b>packer (110/hour) is the bottleneck</b>: 110 × 3,800 × 97% = 405.5k good cases, more than demand, so Riverbend can supply all 400k.</p> <p>Extra cases: 31.4k × $4 = <b>$126k a year</b>. Payback: $230k ÷ $126k = <b>1.8 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> a good investment, and the new bottleneck still leaves headroom above demand.</p>"},{"q":"Is there a cheaper way to get the same output?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Run the filler through breaks</b> with a relief operator: a few more hours a day on the bottleneck only</li> <li><b>Cut changeover time</b> between bottle sizes on the filler</li><li><b>Weekend shift</b> for the filler with a small buffer of filled bottles</li></ul> <p>These could close part of the gap within weeks; the upgrade is the durable fix.</p>"}],"reco":"Approve the filler upgrade. The filler is the bottleneck today, limiting output to about 368.6k good cases against 400k demand. Making it 17% faster moves the bottleneck to the packer, which still has enough capacity to meet demand, adding about $126k of contribution a year and paying back in 1.8 years. Meanwhile, run the filler through breaks to recover some volume now. Risk: faster filling could raise reject rates. Next step: trial the upgrade's speed on one product before committing.","great":["Finds the bottleneck from station speeds","Checks what becomes the bottleneck after the upgrade","Caps output at demand","Suggests quick wins on the bottleneck itself"],"id":47,"slug":"riverbend-bottling"}